      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## When to use\nCheck remote vault health \u2014 orphan notes, dangling links, graph density, methodology grounding, MOC coverage, processing stats. Saves results to the bai/health-report document. All checks run against the live reactor via Switchboard CLI.\n\n## What it covers\n- Pre-flight\n- Step 1: Gather metrics from the subgraph\n- Step 2: Read individual note state\n- Step 3: Check methodology grounding via note content\n- Step 4: Check MOC coverage\n- Step 5: Compute diagnostic checks\n- Step 6: Save to bai/health-report document\n- Step 7: Auto-repair (if `--fix` or user requests)\n- Step 8: Report to user\n- Stranded sources\n- What belongs in `recommendations`\n- Scope methodology grounding honestly\n- Re-run after every fix\n- Reading health history\n\n## Where the full skill lives\n- Vault source: **Agent skill: health** (full SKILL.md text, DERIVED_FROM below)\n- Canonical copy: plugin repo `skills/health/SKILL.md` \u2014 always execute from the repo copy; this note is the discovery layer.\n\n## Invocation\n`/powerhouse-knowledge:health` in Claude Code (plugin installed), or read the source content and follow it manually.\n\n_Synced by sync-skills; source hash sha256:7867bc4c771e\u2026_",
